<?xml version="1.0" standalone='no'?>
<!DOCTYPE service-group SYSTEM "avahi-service.dtd">
<!--
  HaoTranNAS mDNS announcement for avahi (static fallback). Author: Hao Tran

  Normally NOT needed: haotrannas-server announces itself (mdns-sd, config
  mdns_enabled = true) and shares UDP 5353 with avahi-daemon (SO_REUSEPORT;
  checked on the dev PC with avahi running). Use this file only if the two
  conflict on the NAS (phones and `haotrannas-cli discover` find nothing
  while the server runs):
    1. set `mdns_enabled = false` in /etc/haotrannas/config.toml, restart
    2. fill name, port and fp below
    3. sudo cp nas/avahi/haotrannas.service /etc/avahi/services/
       (avahi picks up the folder by itself)
    4. check from another PC on the LAN: haotrannas-cli discover

  Same records as the server (protocol/spec.md section 13):
    name  = server_name from config.toml (default "haotrannas")
    port  = the port of listen_address (default 47100)
    v=1   = protocol version
    fp    = first 16 lowercase hex chars of the server fingerprint

  fp: `haotrannas-server init` prints only the short server id (first 12
  hex chars in groups, e.g. 3F9A-C21B-77E0): too short. The fingerprint is
  the SHA-256 of the server certificate (DER), so on the NAS run:
    openssl x509 -in /srv/haotrannas/tls/server.crt -outform DER | sha256sum | cut -c1-16
  Check: its first 12 chars equal the short id without dashes, in lower
  case. fp changes only if tls/ is made again (then every device pairs
  again and this file needs the new value).

  Difference to the server's own announcement: the SRV target is the NAS
  host name (<hostname>.local), whose avahi records may include AAAA.
  Clients use the IPv4 A record only, so that is harmless.
-->
<service-group>
  <name>haotrannas</name>
  <service protocol="ipv4">
    <type>_haotrannas._tcp</type>
    <port>47100</port>
    <txt-record>v=1</txt-record>
    <txt-record>fp=0000000000000000</txt-record>
  </service>
</service-group>
